n: 9.5.6.20
kind: review
re: 3.6.3.5
saw: 2243cbc0
ack: node
is: (1) 'Every rebuild changes the builder identity' is a record of 2026-09-12 that the present source no longer shows: a store-built kernel 'names itself by the digest of the seed it was made from and the target it runs on', and only a plain cc build follows its executable bytes (fkwu-uni.c:28164-28193). (2) 5.1 GiB is a total, not a figure for each checkout: the note says a design agent's 40 GB figure 'was relative to the CURRENT loader: judged per checkout only 5.1 GiB' (memory/project-fkwu-version-store-2026-11-09.md:26).
why: The record is memory/reference-fkwu-import-lane-vs-flat.md:11-16. A plain build started inside a checkout is replaced by the store's build (fkwu-uni.c:33705-33707), so identity now changes when the runtime's source changes, not at each rebuild.
limit: These hold: lowered text not deterministic on one host (memory/project-prebuilt-design-2026-11-09.md:15); 7,329 of 7,403 entries on 2026-09-12 (memory/reference-fkwu-heat-boards-burial.md:11, which adds that a later commit removes ended processes' boards); five files left with caching off (study/r1/runtime-jit.md:260-261).
by: r3/review-fkwu-runtime
at: 2026-11-24

